      answer: "b",
      explanation: "The dartos is smooth muscle in the scrotal wall and changes skin tension and wrinkling. The cremaster is skeletal muscle that changes testicular position; the tunica albuginea and germinal epithelium do not actively wrinkle scrotal skin.",
      sectionId: "reproduction-testis-position", source: { document: "biology", page: 117 }, cognitive: "application"
